KZ3 patch 2171 (RSX pass 155): capture gaps for the Level 1 replay harness (tools/smoke/test_log_replay.c); renderer step 0.
Applies on top of 2164-2166. Everything is under LD_FIFO_CAPTURE (off = unchanged call stream: one load + predicted branch per hook).
- Gap 1: renderer-side guest writes. WORD tag 11 = a report value ld_rb_drain wrote into guest memory (ea = main-memory IO offset + 8);
  RANGE kind RSX_FC_WR_RENDERER (3) = a surface write-back stored by ld_writeback_surface / ld_rb_store (digest only).
- Gap 2: SPU_NOTE async field 2 = PPU store note (gcm_ppu_note_pages_ea), async 0 = the walker's own NV0039 note.
- Gap 3: WORD tags 12 (ring JUMP written by a recycle / segment-next), 13 (command-context word), 14 (put) at the walker's recycle
  and gcm_fifo_next_segment / the title-ring recycle.
- Gap 6: rsx_fc_range_check() in rsx_fifo_capture.h, the reader-side digest-vs-bytes check.
- RD_RENDERER RANGE records carry in their reserved word 1 = read while sink_end ran (g_rsx_fcap_in_draw), 0 = read outside a draw end.
- rsx_fc_hook: the writer's observer (NULL in the game), the lock-step replay driver's hook.
Format stays version 1 (new tag/kind values, a formerly zero reserved word).

